
Write a C program to demonstrate the order of execution of
operators in an expression using operator precedence and
associativity.

Program

#include<stdio.h>;
int main()
{
int a = 10, b = 5, c = 2;
int result;
result = a + b * c;
printf(&quot;Expression: a + b * c\n&quot;);
printf(&quot;a = %d, b = %d, c = %d\n&quot;, a, b, c);
printf(&quot;Result = %d\n&quot;, result);
return 0;
}

